# SABOTAGE: D-05 (ADR-048 §8 `P8`, operator ruling D-05) — the DURABLE CANCEL CHECK before
# the SUMMARIZING fold is REMOVED from `Samen.AI.Agent.derive_fold/8`. This is the
# sabotage-241 shape ONE MECHANISM AND ONE LEVEL over: 241 removes the cancel re-check at
# the TURN boundary in `loop/5`, so a cancel landing between turn N and turn N+1 is silently
# ignored; THIS removes it inside `derive_fold/8`, on the `span ->` arm, immediately before
# `summarize_fold/7` → `summarize_span/3` — so a cancel landing DURING the overflowing
# attempt is silently ignored and the LEVEL 2 INLINE fold ships the tenant's folded
# conversation to the provider FOR SUMMARIZATION after the tenant has already asked to stop.
# D-05's ruling is that the harm is the EGRESS, not the turn.
#
# Flips the named D-05 red. Everything else stays GREEN, which is what makes the red mean
# what it says: the D-05 ARM 2 POSITIVE CONTROL (the byte-identical script WITHOUT the
# cancel, whose LEVEL 2 fold DOES summarize and IS recorded model-written) still passes, and
# the D-05 ARM 3 PRESERVATION CONTROL (RP-AG-8: the in-flight turn still completes and the
# run takes its terminal at the NEXT turn boundary) still passes — so the red fails because
# the CANCEL check is gone, not because Level 2, the summarizer, or cancel itself broke.
#
# NOT TOUCHED, deliberately: the BREAKER path (`Breaker.killed?(run.org_id, run.agent)` stays
# checked at BOTH the turn boundary and the retry boundary, exactly as P5/D-04 shipped it —
# sabotage 322 owns that clause), the deterministic `reuse_fold!/5` replay arm (no model
# call, no data leaves — D-05 says it is NOT to be guarded), `fold_span/6`'s pure span
# SELECTION, and the whole body of `summarize_fold/7`, which is left byte-for-byte alone.
#
# Deletes ONE CONTIGUOUS `if/else` and its comment, replacing it with the `else` branch's own
# single call, AND the `cancel_requested?/1` predicate the `if` was the only caller of — both
# inside one hunk. Removing the predicate is not extra scope, it is what "the check is gone"
# means here: leaving an uncalled private function behind trips Elixir's unused-private
# warning under `--warnings-as-errors` and the patch would fail to COMPILE instead of failing
# the named test (an `if false do` shape would trip the always-same-result warning the same
# way). Touches agent.ex ALONE.
# APP: samen_core
# TEST_FILES: test/ai/agent_durability_test.exs
